 "policy": "verbatim copies of LICENSE, README.md, requirements.txt, config/ (agent/default.yaml, env/atari.yaml, trainer.yaml), results/data/DIAMOND.json (per-game, per-seed Atari 100k returns of the paper; the G-fid band source) and src/ except src/game/ and src/play.py (pygame interactive UI; the fidelity runner mirrors play.py's pretrained-checkpoint loading in its own code). No edits. The official code runs from vendor/src on sys.path (as upstream `python src/main.py`) in env b127-diamond (G-port reference, fidelity runner). The NovPhy adapter (novphy env) loads src/models/blocks.py and src/models/diffusion/{inner_model,denoiser,diffusion_sampler}.py by file location; denoiser.py's two top-level imports (`from data import Batch`, `from utils import LossAndLogs`) are satisfied during that load only by vendor src/data/batch.py (+ segment.py) and a module holding the upstream `LossAndLogs` alias, because upstream utils.py imports omegaconf / wandb, which novphy lacks. Not vendored: scripts/ (resume.sh, import_run.py), src/game/, src/play.py, .gitignore.",
